#: ../chapter03.rst:5
msgid "Tenant Administration"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:9
msgid "A tenant is usually mapped to a company, or a division of a company, an organization or in the case of MSP managed organization, a service provider would call them clients. Basically, a tenant is a management scope that represents an organization."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:11
msgid "Tenant manager scope is defined for tenant administrators. For a multi-tenant Cluster Server system, each tenant has an administrator. For a single-tenant Cluster Server system, the default cluster administrator is also the tenant administrator."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:13
msgid "Tenant Manager is completely web-based."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:15
msgid "From the Cluster Manager Dashboard, you can access the Tenant Manager by clicking \"Tenants Count\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:20
msgid "CLUSTER DASHBOARD"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:22
msgid "You can also log in directly to the web portal as the tenant administrator instead of the default cluster administrator to get to the tenant administrator management web interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:26
msgid "At a high level, the Cluster Administrator and Tenant Manager have almost identical controls for the Tenants within their scope; however, the Tenant Manager settings will always take precedence and override Cluster Administrator settings. Tenant Managers can give permission for Cluster Administrator to manage their tenants by enabling this option in ``Settings`` > ``User Account & Security`` > ``Security``. \"Allow Cluster Admin to manage my tenant\" is by default checked."
msgstr ""

