msgid "**Do not show file in-place editing/preview disabled notifications**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1603
msgid "This feature also shows file change notifications at the lower right-hand corner of the Windows desktop. People may find it annoying if the change notification comes in quite often."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1605
msgid "**Enable Inplace Open Zip File**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1607
msgid "Windows Explorer has a zip built-in extension that can open a zip file when double-clicked on. It may be good for the local drive but for cloud drive, that means the zip file is unzipped and re-upload back into the cloud. By default client application disables opening zip files directly in the cloud drive."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1609
msgid "**Enable Single Sign On with login windows user identity**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1611
msgid "Enable Single Sign-On with Login Windows User Identity - For a Windows client agent running on a Windows Desktop machine, the login windows user's identity will be used for single sign-on to the |prodname| account."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1613
msgid "**Max Size of Zip File Allowed to Open In-place (MB)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1615
msgid "Limits the size of a Zip File that can be opened in-place."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1617
msgid "**Max Size of File Allowed to Generate Thumbnail (MB)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1619
msgid "Limits the size of Files that can be used in the generation of thumbnails."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1621
msgid "**Cloud Drive Label**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1623
msgid "What do you want to call your windows client drive."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1625
msgid "**Drive Letter**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1627
msgid "What do you want to give the drive letter to the client application."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1629
msgid "**Cache Size Limit (MB)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1631
msgid "The Windows client maintains a client-side cache of this size (0 - unlimited)"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1633
msgid "**Minimal free disk space (GB)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1635
msgid "This setting is used to establish a minimum amount of disk space used for the windows client drive."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1637
msgid "**Purge logging db n days old (0 - don't purge)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1639
msgid "This limits how many days of logging are kept in the Windows client cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1641
msgid "**Mount Drive in global space (Windows Client Only)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1643
msgid "A drive mounted in the global space will not be subject to UAC (User Account Control) limitations, such as when legacy applications are required to run with administrative privilege and cannot see the drive guarded by the UAC. On the other hand, drives that are mounted in the global space are visible to any other users who log in on the same Windows machine at the same time."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1645
msgid "**In offline mode, only show files that are cached and available locally**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1647
msgid "Typically there will be place-holder files and representative icons created for all of the files in the client drive. If this setting is enabled, only locally stored files will be shown."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1649
msgid "**Disable \"Check Out\"**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1651
msgid "Turn off the \"Check Out\" feature and remove it from the right-click context menu."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1653
msgid "**Encrypt Local Cache**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1655
msgid "Once enabled, when a file is downloaded to cache, it is encrypted in place. When an authorized user then accesses the file from the (M:) Mapped Cloud Drive, CentreStack automatically decrypts it on the fly and then returns it to the user."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1657
msgid "**Disable AutoCad Optimization**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1659
msgid "By default, there is an AutoCAD optimization that delays the synchronization of the updated .dwg file and schedules it to sync upwards to the cloud at a later time. Use this setting to disable this AutoCad optimization and make saving AutoCAD .dwg files act the same as saving other regular files and lets .dwg file behavior follow other policy settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1663
msgid "Large File Upload"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1667
msgid "LARGE FILE UPLOAD SETTINGS"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1669
msgid "**Enable chunk uploading when file size larger than (MB)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1671
msgid "Uploading a single large file can be disrupted by an Internet glitch. This setting breaks large files into smaller chunks to increase the success rate."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1673
msgid "**Chunk file in the unit of (MB)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1675
msgid "Works with the above setting to establish what size the chunks will be in as they are transferred."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1677
msgid "**Use Volume Shadow Copy to Upload Files being Opened**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1679
msgid "There is pro and con of using this flag. When file is open by other application, the file usually is locked and can't be uploaded until the file is closed. However using volume shadow copy can still upload the file. The down side is when the volume shadow copy happens, the file is not known to be in a consistent state."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1683
msgid "Bandwidth Control"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1687
msgid "BANDWIDTH CONTROL SETTINGS"
msgstr ""

