msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1795
msgid "**Confirm before moving via drag-and-drop**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1797
msgid "In web portal, sometimes there can be accidental drag and drop, in this case, having a confirmation dialog can help prevent accidental drag and drop."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1799
msgid "**Show left tree view by default**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1801
msgid "Disabled by default. When enabled left-tree is displayed when you log in to the web portal."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1803
msgid "**Do not show \"recent activities**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1805
msgid "Disabled by default. When enabled \"recent activities\" is not visible in the Show/Hide Info Panel on the right side of the Web Portal File Browser."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1807
msgid "**Show 'link to local' option to non-admin user**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1809
msgid "Disabled by default. When enabled, non-admin user will have access to the **\"Link to Local\"** option in the Sharing and Collaboration tab under the Show/Hide Info Panel on the right side of the Web Portal File Browser."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1811
msgid "**Show max count of file/folder items**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1813
msgid "Default files to show is 1,000. Some customers may have a very flat folder that has more than one thousand files. It is not recommended to have a cloud system have flat folder structure like this. But if customer has many files in a flat folder. This setting can be used to show all files by increasing this number as needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1817
msgid "Native Client"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1819
msgid "``Tenant Manager`` > ``Settings`` >  ``Clients & Applications`` > ``Native Client``"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1824
msgid "NATIVE CLIENT SETTINGS"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1826
msgid "**Create a shortcut in the documents library**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1828
msgid "Enabled by default. This is a convenience feature to add a link to documents library to the cloud drive."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1830
msgid "**Create shortcut on desktop**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1832
msgid "Enabled by default. Same as above but the shortcut is on the desktop."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1834
msgid "**Hide Settings in Windows Client Management Console**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1836
msgid "Disabled by default. The Settings in the Windows client may be viewed as “too much information for normal user”. If that is the case, enabling this option will hide those settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1838
msgid "**Don't Allow Setting Changes in Windows Client Management Console**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1840
msgid "Disabled by default. When disabled the Windows Client user can change the settings in the Windows Client Management Console."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1842
msgid "**Disable Windows client in-place drag & drop uploading**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1844
msgid "Unchecked by default. When enabled, dragging & dropping files (or folders) to the cloud drive will write files to the local cache first and then upload in the background."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1846
msgid "**Disable Auto-Login next time**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1848
msgid "Unchecked by default. When you want the user to type in username/password every time they login to the Windows client, you can check this to disable auto-login."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1850
msgid "**Disable drag & drop handler**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1852
msgid "Unchecked by default. If you check this option, the Windows file drag and drop will take over, this typically means the files will be copied into cache before upload, thus resulting in two copies of files being uploaded."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1854
msgid "**Requiring approval for device access**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1856
msgid "Disabled by default. When a user attempts to log in from a new device via native client applications, the connection will be rejected until the tenant admin approves the new device. The approval can be done from the \"Client Device Manager\""
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1858
msgid "**Enable auto-install of Outlook Plugin**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1860
msgid "Disabled by default. The Cluster Server Windows Desktop client comes with an Outlook plug-in. If this option is enabled, the Outlook plugin will be enabled upon client startup."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1862
msgid "**Disable native client for guest users**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1864
msgid "Unchecked by default. For guest users, don't allow them to use native client, so the guest users can only use web browser files and folder view."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1869
msgid "Folder & Storage"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1872
msgid "Backend Storage"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1874
msgid "``Tenant Manager`` > ``Settings`` >  ``Folder & Storage`` > ``Backend Storage``"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1876
msgid "Each tenant has a default backend storage. Tenant user (team user)'s home storage and other shared storage space can be allocated from the default backend storage."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1881
msgid "You can think of the Tenant Backend Storage as a \"Black Box\" managed by the Cluster Server and you shall always use the Cluster Server interface to interact with the content inside the storage. If you can't take this \"Black Box\" approach for the tenant's root backend storage, you can use the following other methods via the team folders, such as import file server network share."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1883
msgid "However, if you already have a file server that will provide the storage, it is recommended to use \"Import Network File Shares\" to mount the file server network share to the tenant's storage space. In this case, you can leave the \"Default Storage\" as is, or point it to an empty location and treat it as a black box storage managed at the Cluster Server level."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1888
msgid "STORAGE MANAGER ACCESS"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1890
msgid "To access the Tenant Storage Manager, click \"Folder & Storage\" on \"Settings\" section. To check the backend storage information, click the dropdown at the top right corner, and select \"Edit\", to edit the storage configuration details."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1892
msgid "If cluster admin needs to check the backend storage for multiple tenants, go to \"Tenant Manager\". Click the \"hamburger\" menu at the top right corner of each tenant, and then choose \"Edit Existing Default Storage\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1897
msgid "STORAGE MANAGER ACCESS - MULTIPLE TENANTS"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1902
msgid "You can mount different storage services into a single namespace (folder structure). For example, if you have multiple Amazon S3 buckets, you can mount them all in. If you have multiple OpenStack Swift accounts, you can mount them all in as well. If you have multiple file server network shares, you can add them to the storage manager."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1906
msgid "The cluster manager can define whether or not the Storage Manager is exposed to the tenant administrator."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1911
msgid "EDITING STORAGE SETTINGS"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1914
msgid "Edit Local Storage"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1916
msgid "This is the file server UNC path or local windows folder path that you will connect into the tenant administrator's root folder structure. The idea here is you will take this folder and mount the folder to the tenant administrator's root folder structure."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1921
msgid "The user name is the Windows username, either it being local Windows user or global Active Directory user, this is a Windows account that is capable of accessing the \"Local Storage Location\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1926
msgid "This is the password for the Windows user above."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1930
msgid "We recommend this Windows user and his credential be set up as a service account, meaning the password isn't subject to the maximum password days via local security policy. The reason being, that, when it is time to rotate or change the user password, the connection here may be broken until the password is updated to match."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1933
msgid "**“Always access the storage using logon user identity”**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1935
msgid "When you have Active Directory Integration, and mount an existing file server network share in, you can select “Always access the storage using logon user identity” so the ACL (NTFS Permission) on the file server share will be used natively. The access permission will be checked natively against the user's Active Directory identity that is defined by the NTFS permission."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1937
msgid "This option only applies to the \"Local Storage\" such as network share, DFS share, local folder, and etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1939
msgid "**“The share is from a Linux/Unix/ZFS server”**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1941
msgid "Most of the time, you don't want to check this flag because your file server share shall behave like a normal Windows Server share, even if it doesn't come from a Windows Server."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1943
msgid "In some small SOHO network storage devices, it may only allow one connection from one IP address, so if that is the case, you want to check this flag. Most of the time, you just don't need to check this when the network share is capable of taking multiple connections/sessions from one single machine."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1945
msgid "**“This share is a DFS share”**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1947
msgid "If the share is a DFS share, you will check this checkbox, because DFS share has an extra layer of translation to translate back down to normal file server shares. This flag tells the Cluster Server to do an extra DFS translation back to SMB share before connecting to the share."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1949
msgid "**“Enable Inplace Versioning”**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1951
msgid "The underlying file server network share may not have explicit version control (it may have volume shadow copy for other purposes). This will add Cluster Server version control to the file server network share. It is independent of and not related to the volume shadow copy."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1955
msgid "In place versioning will put the older version of the file into a __ver__ subfolder in the same folder structure making the name for In-Place Versioning so the folder structure is maintained as-is, while extra old copies of the file will be stored in a specific subfolder."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1960
msgid "IN-PLACE VERSIONING"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1962
msgid "Here is a demo video showing the result of \"Enable Inplace Versioning\" when the root folder ('forward slash') is mounted with the \"Inplace versioning\" enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1971
msgid "Migrate to New Storage"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1976
msgid "CLOUD STORAGE MIGRATE"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1978
msgid "Once the tenant backend storage is set, we don't recommend changing it until it has to be changed (e.g., migrate to other location). However when you are just setting up the tenant, you can decide where your tenant's storage location is and can change between local file server storage or remote cloud storage service."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1980
msgid "There are two types of storage migrations."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1986
msgid "**1.** Migrate data to a different location in the same type of storage:"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1983
msgid "Identify the location of the current storage"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1984
msgid "Copy the content to the new location (for example, you can use xcopy *.* from the old location to the new location"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1985
msgid "Login to web portal as Cluster Admin."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1986
msgid "Go to Tenant Manager -> Manage the specific Tenant -> Backend Storage and click on edit to point to the new location"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1991
msgid "**2.**  Migrate data to a different type of storage:"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1989
msgid "Go to the registry using regedit"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1990
msgid "Go to HKLM\\\\SOFTWARE\\\\Gladinet\\\\Enterprise\\\\ and add a new string value called 'CanChangeDefaultStorage' and set the value to 'True' and reboot"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1991
msgid "Edit the storage type using new icon to edit storage under Cluster Manager\\Tenant Manager"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1995
msgid "It is not recommended that you modify registry settings. Create a backup of the registry before modifying any registry settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:1998
msgid "Retention Policy"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2000
msgid "``Tenant Manager`` > ``Settings`` > ``Folder & Storage`` > ``Retention Policy``"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2006
msgid "RETENTION POLICY SETTINGS"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2008
msgid "The cloud monitoring service on the Cluster Server will be responsible for the retention policy. The settings of the retention policy are described below."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2010
msgid "**Keep last n version(s) of files in versioned folder**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2012
msgid "This setting lets you decide how many versions of files to keep in the version folder. (0 - let system decide, also apply to \"attached local folder')"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2014
msgid "**Only purge versioned files that are more than n day(s) old**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2016
msgid "This is a security feature. For example, there is a virus modified the same file many times so it created many versions causing good old versions to be scheduled for deletion. However, with this set, the good old versions will be kept for at least the amount of days so give enough time to recover. (0 - purge old versions once they exceed the version limit, regardless of the version lifespan)"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2018
msgid "**Keep deleted files in versioned folder and/or Trash Can for n day(s)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2020
msgid "When a file is deleted in the version folder, it is not actually deleted. It will be kept for several days defined here. The same policy also apply to"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2022
msgid "**Keep file change log for n day(s)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2024
msgid "File change log is the biggest database table and could be growing without trimming. You can decide how often you want to trim the table."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2028
msgid "There is also a cluster setting about the file change log length. The cluster setting overrides the per-tenant setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2030
msgid "**Keep audit trace for n day(s)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2032
msgid "Audit trace log is stored in a local device directory and keeps a record of high-level activity from a device (e.g., windows client, server agent). This setting limits the number of days that are stored in the local database file."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2034
msgid "**Hide purge option from web file browser (not applicable to tenant administrator)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2036
msgid "Do not show the purge window to users when deleting content."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2038
msgid "**Don't send email notifications when purging deleted content**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2040
msgid "There are times when an admin would not want to send or see delete email notifications for purged contents."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2042
msgid "**Include deleted but not yet purged items in storage quota**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2044
msgid "Allows you to decide if you want to include not visible (purged) files in the storage quota that is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2047
msgid "Folder and Storage"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2049
msgid "``Tenant Manager`` > ``Settings`` > ``Folder & Storage`` > ``Folder and Storage``"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2051
msgid "These are the settings available to the tenant manager in the Folder and Storage view."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2056
msgid "FOLDER AND STORAGE SETTINGS"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2059
msgid "**Allow users to attach external cloud storage**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2061
msgid "When checked, you will allow users to see storage manager and allow them to attach external storage such as their own Amazon S3 bucket into the system."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2064
msgid "**Disable Versioned folder**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2066
msgid "Normally you will NOT disable versioned folder. Because versioned folder is the supporting feature for “Two-way sync locally attached folder”. If you disable versioned folder, you will lose the two-way synchronization folder feature as well."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2070
msgid "**Disable Trash Can**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2072
msgid "For folders that are not under version control, a deleted file will be moved into Trash Can. If this feature is not useful, you can disable it."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2076
msgid "**Don't show folder that user doesn't have read permission**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2078
msgid "With native Active Directory integration and with network share as backend storage, the user's permission to the folders are checked natively. When this option is set, for those folders that users doesn't have read permission, the folder will be hidden."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2082
msgid "**Don't show team folder that the user doesn't have read permission to the underlying folder**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2084
msgid "In the folder listing, if the user don't have read permission, sometimes it is better off not to show the folder to the user."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2087
msgid "**Don't show Trash Can for non-admin user**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2089
msgid "Trash Can is a virtual folder that shows up at the web browser portal only. This setting controls whether or not to show it for regular team user."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2093
msgid "**Don't append (Team Folder) to published folders**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2095
msgid "A team folder by default, when showing up in a team user's folder list, it will have “(Team Folder)” appended to the end of the folder name to signify it is a team folder. This feature allows a team folder showing up as it is without the (Team Folder) suffix. The use case is that when a network share is mounted and then turned into a team folder, since the users are already familiar with the network share in its original name, so it is not necessary to append (team folder) to the folder name. You shouldn't change this setting in the middle of operation because if users have pending upload/download, changing the name could cause those tasks to fail."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2105
msgid "Attached Folder"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2107
msgid "``Tenant Manager`` > ``Settings`` > ``Folder & Storage`` > ``Attached Folder``"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2112
msgid "ATTACHED FOLDER SETTINGS"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2115
msgid "**Disable backup/attach local folder from client device**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2117
msgid "Attached Local Folders are two-way synchronization folders. In order to do version backup and two-way synchronization, there are multiple folder structures created in the backend storage. Some organization doesn't need this feature and want the users to work exclusively with the cloud drive."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2122
msgid "**Enable Snapshot backup for server agent**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2124
msgid "It is a feature related to server agent on Windows 2003-2012 servers."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2126
msgid "**Allow syncing empty files**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2128
msgid "By default, empty file (0-byte) will be skipped for syncing in attached folder. when enabled, those files will be synchronized."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2131
msgid "**Allow syncing of hidden files**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2133
msgid "Hidden files by default will not sync."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2135
msgid "**Allow executable files (.exe)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2137
#: ../chapter03.rst:2141
msgid "Executable files by default will not sync."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2139
msgid "**Allow ISO files (.iso)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2143
msgid "**Allow backup files(.bck, .bkf,.rbf, .tib)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2145
msgid "**Allow VMs (.hdd, .hds, .pvm, .pvs, .vdi, .vfd, .vhd, .vmc, .vmdk, .vmem, .vmsd, .vmsn, .vmss, .vmtm, .vmwarevm, .vmx, .vmxf, .vsv, .nvram, .vud, .xva)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2147
msgid "**Allow application folders**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2149
msgid "Application folder by default will not sync."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2151
msgid "**Allow application data folders**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2153
msgid "Application data folder by default will not sync."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2155
msgid "**Enable scheduled sync for files with following extensions**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2157
msgid "This is to help sync/upload frequently changed file such as Microsoft access database or QuickBook files. These type of files typically are constantly open (thus prevent other application to hold on to them) and also changed frequently. So you can define the time period to check back on these type of files and use volume shadow copy to upload these files."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2166
msgid "Filters"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2168
msgid "``Tenant Manager`` > ``Settings`` > ``Folder & Storage`` > ``Filters``"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2173
msgid "FILTER SETTINGS"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2175
msgid "**Files with the following extensions will be excluded from attached local folder**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2177
msgid "You can stop certain file types from being uploaded. For example .pst files. These are local outlook email files, which is not necessary to upload into the cloud storage because usually it is backed up by an exchange server."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2182
msgid "**Files with following extensions will be excluded from directory listing (i.e.[.qbw])**"
