#: ../chapter03.rst:2189
msgid "Windows Explorer has a habit to peek into large files to generate thumbnail and present other information. It may not be a good fit for cloud drive files because each peek will generate a download from cloud."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2193
msgid "**Allow file without file name extension**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2195
msgid "Allow files without extension suffix to synchronize."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2198
msgid "**Allow syncing empty file**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2200
msgid "This is the same setting as in the \"Attached Folder\" section."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2204
msgid "Background Tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2206
msgid "``Tenant Manager`` > ``Settings`` > ``Folder & Storage`` > ``Background Tasks``"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2208
msgid "There are three different kind of background tasks that may take a long time to finish:"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2210
msgid "Data Seeding - copying data into |prodname|"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2211
msgid "Storage Scan - do a full scan to calculate storage consumption"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2212
msgid "Tenant Storage Migration - move tenant storage from location A to location B"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2213
msgid "Anchor Migration -  move data out of Anchor and into |prodname|"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2219
msgid "BACKGROUND TASKS"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2221
msgid "The cluster administrator can help the tenant seed the data. For example take data into a USB drive and take it to the same local area network as the Cluster Server and see the data into the tenant storage."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2224
msgid "**Add New Data Seeding Task**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2226
msgid "``Background Tasks`` > ``+`` > ``Add New Data Seeding Task``"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2231
msgid "DATA SEEDING"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2233
msgid "Data Seeding is to take a folder from a source location and seed it into a team folder."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2235
msgid "On the left of the dialog, it is the source folder path information."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2237
msgid "On the right side of the dialog, it is the target team folder information."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2239
msgid "If you are seeding the data into a brand new team folder, you will first go into the team folder area and create a new team folder with empty content inside, and then come back to data seeding page and select it from the team folder drop down."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2244
msgid "Tenant Branding"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2246
msgid "``Tenant Manager`` > ``Branding`` > ``Tenant Branding``"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2248
msgid "The cluster administrator can help the tenant do the tenant-specific branding in the partner portal."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2250
msgid "The branding is applied by the customized URL. You can think of the customized URL as a primary key to retrieve all tenant related branding information."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2255
msgid "If per-tenant branding is enabled, The tenant branding section will be available."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2260
msgid "PER-TENANT BRANDING OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2262
msgid "**Customized URL for your business**"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2264
msgid "Typically the customize URL is a sub domain of the Cluster Server. For example, if the Cluster Server is at https://cloud.mycompany.com, the sub domain can be https://acme1.mycompany.com"
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2266
msgid "In Windows 2012 and above (the server that has the Cluster Server running), it also allows SNI (Server name indicator) in the SSL certificate binding. So it is possible to bind multiple SSL certificates to the same IIS server. In this case, the Customized URL can be a fully qualified domain name."
msgstr ""

#: ../chapter03.rst:2270
msgid "If you set up per-tenant branding, make sure the customized URL is specific to each tenant and also the URL is different from the default URL."
